35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our costs are quite volatile; February was nearly triple August. Furthermore, some rooms are naturally colder than others. We must ensure our system doesn't penalize those who simply have a draftier room.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh wow, I looked into those templates and other houses, and it sounds like a nightmare! Even with a template, it's so much manual work. I'm worried that if we go too detailed, someone will spend their whole evening on it!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The data from the monitors shows a significant disparity in energy use, with some rooms drawing four times more than others. This confirms that a flat split may be causing the imbalances some of us suspect.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The volatility is indeed concerning; the statements show no two consecutive months are even within 4,000 yen of each other. Additionally, installing sub-meters would be quite expensive, costing 34,000 yen per room plus annual maintenance fees.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I saw that some payments were very late, and people got confused about the amounts. It took a long time to agree on what the new people owed too. I think this is why we've been feeling tense.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are facing a classic dilemma: the desire for mathematical precision versus the need for social harmony. If we track every watt, we risk turning our home into an accounting firm, which sounds dreadfully tedious.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! @Benjamin, you hit the nail on the head. If we spend hours every month calculating tiny differences, we'll just end up stressed. We need a system that's fast and doesn't feel like a second job!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"While I value simplicity, we cannot ignore that some are paying for others' heavy usage. If we prioritize speed over fairness, the resentment Minato noticed in the payment logs will only continue to grow.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, I understand the need for fairness, but we must be realistic. Spending over 130,000 yen on sub-meters is a significant upfront cost that could create its own financial strain. We need a solution that balances equity without being prohibitively expensive.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, I agree that fairness is important. But if we focus too much on who used what, will we just find more things to be angry about? I want us to stop feeling tense.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Perhaps we should consider a system that provides a predictable baseline. If we avoid the ""accounting firm"" approach but acknowledge the room disparities, we can ensure no one feels forced to shiver in a coat to save money.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I love the idea of a predictable baseline! If we can just set a fixed amount or a simple rule, we won't have to spend hours on spreadsheets. Let's pick the easiest way to manage it!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"A predictable baseline is a start, but it must be grounded in the reality of our usage. If we ignore the four-fold difference in energy draw, we are simply choosing a different way to be unfair.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, we cannot ignore the data, but we also cannot ignore the budget. A system that is perfectly fair on paper but costs us a fortune to implement or hours to manage is not sustainable. We need a middle ground.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"Maybe we can find a way that doesn't require us to check every little thing? If the rules are clear and simple from the start, maybe we won't have to argue or feel bad about asking for money.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. We must be honest: a system that is too rigid may lead to a cold house and cold hearts. Let us hope the proposed options offer a balance between fairness and comfort.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm with you, Benjamin! Let's hope the options are super simple. I really don't want any of us spending our free time doing boring math. Let's find the one that's the least amount of work!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I hope the options allow us to address the usage gap without creating an administrative burden. If we can find a way to tie payments to actual consumption simply, we can finally put these rumors of imbalance to rest.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I hope the options provide a way to smooth out those monthly spikes. A system that offers financial predictability without requiring a massive initial investment would be the most rational choice for all of us.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want us to be happy again. If we pick a way that is clear and doesn't make anyone feel accused, maybe we can stop being sad and just enjoy living together.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
