60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is far too simplistic given our volatility, and Option C, while precise, is an expensive administrative nightmare. Option B seems the most elegant; it provides predictability and prevents winter anxiety.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I totally agree with Benjamin! Option C sounds like way too much work, and Option A still means calculating new totals every month. Option B is the winner for me—it's the fastest and easiest!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B is a compromise, but it doesn't solve the core issue of usage disparity. Option C is the only one that ensures objective fairness, though I acknowledge the cost concerns Victoria mentioned.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is financially unfeasible given the high installation costs. Option A leaves us vulnerable to those extreme monthly spikes. Option B is the most rational choice, as it provides the budget stability we need.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option C sounds like it might make us argue about the numbers even more. Option B seems nice because we know what to expect, so we won't have to feel surprised or upset every month.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is quite telling that we are almost in unison. Option B allows us to maintain a comfortable home without the psychological burden of calculating every single yen in real-time. It preserves both our warmth and our friendship.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! @Jonathan, I know you want it to be perfectly fair, but is it really worth spending our whole evening on it? Option B is just so much more relaxed. Let's go with the one that keeps us happy!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I value our harmony, but true peace comes from knowing things are right. If we ignore the disparity, the resentment will simply hide until it boils over. However, I see the consensus.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, while I respect your commitment to fairness, the financial risk of Option C is too high. Option B allows us to plan our budgets and avoids the stress of those unpredictable spikes. It is the most sustainable path.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I think @Jonathan is right that fairness matters, but I'm more worried about us fighting. If we pick Option B, we can just trust each other and be friends. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we have reached a near-consensus, I believe it is time to finalize this. Option B offers the perfect blend of financial predictability and social grace. I shall cast my vote for it.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for Option B too! It's definitely the best way to keep things simple and save us all from a mountain of paperwork. Let's pick the easy way and get back to having fun!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I still believe that ignoring the usage gap is a risk, but I value the peace of this house. To avoid further conflict and maintain our harmony, I will vote for Option B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Option B is the only choice that ensures budget stability and avoids an unreasonable upfront cost. It is the most practical and sustainable solution for all of us. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm so glad we all agree! I want us to be kind to each other and stop worrying about the money. I vote for Option B too!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare and pleasant thing to find such swift unanimity. By choosing Option B, we ensure that our home remains a sanctuary of comfort rather than a ledger of grievances. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so happy we all agree! No more boring math and no more stressful evenings. I vote for Option B! Let's celebrate by doing something fun together!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I hope that by agreeing on this, we can truly move past any lingering doubts. For the sake of our collective peace and friendship, I vote for Option B.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Option B. It is the most rational way to manage our volatility and protect our individual budgets without incurring unnecessary debt. I am glad we found a sustainable solution.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote for Option B too! I'm really happy that we all decided together. Now we can just be happy friends and not feel sad about the bills anymore!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
